  *** PAPER-LIVE -- THE LIVE DECISION PATH, NOTHING SENT ***
  No credentials are loaded, production is never armed, and the
  order path is never reached. Every other rail is the live one:
  at most 1 contract(s) a leg and 5 AGREEING legs a race,
  only inside 60 s, only at 90c or dearer, at most $20.00 open at any moment,
  5 s of confirmation or the clock at 20 s, whichever first.
  It does NOT stop on a loss (stop_on_loss=False) -- an arm that
  halts can never reach the races its bar needs, and it risks
  nothing. The REST last look is skipped (fresh_ask is null).
  ITS FILL RATE IS NOT EVIDENCE: `would_fill` is the smaller
  of what we asked for and what the book was OFFERING, and the
  size we ask for is built from that same number -- so it is
  always 100%. Whether the offer would have been OURS is the
  one thing no paper arm can test, and both real race losses
  filled at prices a once-a-second tape never showed.
  It is also stood down by pinracepenny.stop, the MONEY test's switch.

